# Cloudflare Pages headers, appended after public/_headers.
#
# public/_headers (security headers, long caching for assets) is read the
# same way by Netlify and Cloudflare, so it is reused as-is. This file adds
# the [[headers]] blocks from netlify.toml, which Cloudflare ignores.
# scripts/prepare-cloudflare.mjs joins the two into dist/_headers during a
# Cloudflare build only.
#
# Left out on purpose:
#   - Strict-Transport-Security: public/_headers already sets it on /*.
#     Cloudflare joins repeated headers with a comma, so setting it twice
#     would produce an invalid value.
#   - "X-Robots-Tag: index, follow" on public pages: that is the default
#     when the header is absent, and adding it to /* would merge with the
#     noindex rules below into a contradictory value.
#   - "Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate" on public pages:
#     Cloudflare already sends exactly that for HTML pages.

/admin
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/admin/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/portal
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/portal/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/store/success
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, follow
  Cache-Control: no-store

# Apple Pay domain verification. Stripe checks this file over HTTPS before it
# will show an Apple Pay button. It has no extension, so pin the type. See
# docs/apple-pay.md.
/.well-known/apple-developer-merchantid-domain-association
  ! Content-Type
  Content-Type: text/plain
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
